# Awing AI Learning — fastlane deliver stub configuration.
#
# .github/workflows/build-ios.yml Phase 2 "auto-submit for App Store
# Review" calls `fastlane deliver` from the repo root. Without a
# Deliverfile present, deliver refuses to run and exits with:
#
#   No deliver configuration found in the current directory.
#   Do you want to setup deliver?
#   Could not retrieve response as fastlane runs in non-interactive mode
#
# Session 63 (2026-07-08) discovery: the entire deliver auto-submit
# has been silently broken since Session 61's cactus_util blockage —
# every tag from +94 through +99 failed at cactus_util before ever
# reaching this step, so the missing Deliverfile went unnoticed. Now
# that v1.19.2+100 clears the cactus block and pilot uploads to
# TestFlight successfully, deliver is the next thing to fix.
#
# All actual settings — app_identifier, build_number, submit_for_review,
# automatic_release, skip_binary_upload, skip_metadata, skip_screenshots,
# force — are passed as CLI flags in the workflow file. Values are the
# source of truth there, not here, so we don't duplicate settings in
# both places (drift risk).
#
# The single line below satisfies deliver's config-file-must-exist
# check. app_identifier matches what the workflow already passes on the
# CLI, so setting it here doesn't introduce new behavior.
app_identifier "com.awing.awingAiLearning"
